{"id":"mahabharata-12-210","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":210,"title":"दशाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 210 · The four things to be known","summary":{"en":"The teacher says that he who does not know the fourfold, the manifest and unmanifest, the self and the Supreme, does not know the highest dharma. He tells that the sage Narayana is the source of all, and ends the teaching of the preceptor.","kn":"ವ್ಯಕ್ತ, ಅವ್ಯಕ್ತ, ಆತ್ಮ, ಪರಮ ಎಂಬ ನಾಲ್ಕನ್ನು ತಿಳಿಯದವನು ಪರಮ ಧರ್ಮ ತಿಳಿಯನೆಂದು ಗುರು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಋಷಿ ನಾರಾಯಣನೇ ಎಲ್ಲದರ ಮೂಲವೆಂದು ಹೇಳಿ ಗುರುವಿನ ಬೋಧನೆ ಮುಗಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"गुरु कहते हैं कि जो व्यक्त, अव्यक्त, आत्मा और परम इन चारों को नहीं जानता वह परम धर्म को नहीं जानता। वे कहते हैं कि ऋषि नारायण सबके स्रोत हैं, और गुरु का उपदेश समाप्त करते हैं।","te":"వ్యక్తం, అవ్యక్తం, ఆత్మ, పరమం అనే నాలుగింటిని తెలియనివాడు పరమ ధర్మం తెలియడని గురువు చెబుతాడు. ఋషి నారాయణుడే అన్నిటికీ మూలమని చెప్పి గురు బోధను ముగిస్తాడు.","ta":"வெளிப்பட்டது, வெளிப்படாதது, ஆன்மா, பரம் ஆகிய நான்கையும் அறியாதவன் உயர்ந்த தர்மத்தை அறியான் என்று குரு கூறுகிறார். முனிவர் நாராயணனே அனைத்துக்கும் மூலம் என்று கூறிக் குருவின் போதனையை முடிக்கிறார்.","ml":"നാലുവിധമായതും, വ്യക്തവും അവ്യക്തവും, ആത്മാവും പരമാത്മാവും അറിയാത്തവൻ ഉത്തമധർമ്മം അറിയുന്നില്ലെന്ന് ഗുരു പറയുന്നു. സകലത്തിന്റെയും ഉറവിടം മുനി നാരായണനാണെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു; അതോടെ ഗുരുവിന്റെ ഉപദേശം അവസാനിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.210; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"गुरुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The teacher said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"न स वेद परं धर्मं यो न वेद चतुष्टयम् ।\nव्यक्ताव्यक्ते च यत्तत्त्वं संप्राप्तं परमर्षिणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He does not know the supreme dharma who does not know the fourfold truth, and the principle of the manifest and unmanifest that the great sage attained."}},{"n":2,"text":"व्यक्तं मृत्युमुखं विद्यादव्यक्तममृतं पदम् ।\nप्रवृत्तिलक्षणं धर्ममृषिर्नारायणोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know the manifest as the mouth of death and the unmanifest as the immortal state. The sage Narayana declared that dharma is marked by active engagement."}},{"n":3,"text":"अत्रैवावस्थितं सर्वं त्रैलोक्यं सचराचरम् ।\nनिवृत्तिलक्षणं धर्ममव्यक्तं ब्रह्म शाश्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the three worlds, moving and unmoving, rest right here. The dharma marked by withdrawal is the unmanifest, eternal Brahman."}},{"n":4,"text":"प्रवृत्तिलक्षणं धर्मं प्रजापतिरथाब्रवीत् ।\nप्रवृत्तिः पुनरावृत्तिर्निवृत्तिः परमा गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Prajapati declared the dharma marked by engagement. Engagement means return; withdrawal is the highest goal."}},{"n":5,"text":"तां गतिं परमामेति निवृत्तिपरमो मुनिः ।\nज्ञानतत्त्वपरो नित्यं शुभाशुभनिदर्शकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage devoted to withdrawal, always intent on the truth of knowledge, seeing good and evil, reaches that highest goal."}},{"n":6,"text":"तदेवमेतौ विज्ञेयावव्यक्तपुरुषावुभौ ।\nअव्यक्तपुरुषाभ्यां तु यत्स्यादन्यन्महत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So both of these, the unmanifest and the spirit, are to be known; and what is greater than the unmanifest and the spirit is another."}},{"n":7,"text":"तं विशेषमवेक्षेत विशेषेण विचक्षणः ।\nअनाद्यन्तावुभावेतावलिङ्गौ चाप्युभावपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise man should look to that distinction with care. Both of these are without beginning or end, and both are without marks."}},{"n":8,"text":"उभौ नित्यौ सूक्ष्मतरौ महद्भ्यश्च महत्तरौ ।\nसामान्यमेतदुभयोरेवं ह्यन्यद्विशेषणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both are eternal, subtler than the subtle and greater than the great. This is common to both; the rest is how they differ."}},{"n":9,"text":"प्रकृत्या सर्गधर्मिण्या तथा त्रिविधसत्त्वया ।\nविपरीतमतो विद्यात्क्षेत्रज्ञस्य च लक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By nature, which creates and has the three qualities, know that the mark of the knower of the field is the opposite."}},{"n":10,"text":"प्रकृतेश्च विकाराणां द्रष्टारमगुणान्वितम् ।\nअग्राह्यौ पुरुषावेतावलिङ्गत्वादसंहितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the witness of nature and its transformations, free of qualities. These two spirits, being without marks, are ungraspable and unjoined."}},{"n":11,"text":"संयोगलक्षणोत्पत्तिः कर्मजा गृह्यते यया ।\nकरणैः कर्मनिर्वृत्तैः कर्ता यद्यद्विचेष्टते ।\nकीर्त्यते शब्दसंज्ञाभिः कोऽहमेषोऽप्यसाविति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through that by which a birth marked by union, born of action, is grasped, with the instruments that accomplish action, whatever the doer does is named by words: 'Who am I? This is he.'"}},{"n":12,"text":"उष्णीषवान्यथा वस्त्रैस्त्रिभिर्भवति संवृतः ।\nसंवृतोऽयं तथा देही सत्त्वराजसतामसैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a man wearing a turban is covered by three cloths, so this embodied one is covered by sattva, rajas and tamas."}},{"n":13,"text":"तस्माच्चतुष्टयं वेद्यमेतैर्हेतुभिराचितम् ।\nयथासंज्ञो ह्ययं सम्यगन्तकाले न मुह्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the fourfold truth, built up by these reasons, must be known; one who knows it as named does not fall into delusion at the end."}},{"n":14,"text":"श्रियं दिव्यामभिप्रेप्सुर्ब्रह्म वाङ्मनसा शुचिः ।\nशारीरैर्नियमैरुग्रैश्चरेन्निष्कल्मषं तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who desires divine prosperity, pure in speech and mind, should practise stainless austerity with severe bodily disciplines, toward Brahman."}},{"n":15,"text":"त्रैलोक्यं तपसा व्याप्तमन्तर्भूतेन भास्वता ।\nसूर्यश्च चन्द्रमाश्चैव भासतस्तपसा दिवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The three worlds are pervaded by austerity, the shining power within; the sun and the moon shine in heaven by austerity."}},{"n":16,"text":"प्रतापस्तपसो ज्ञानं लोके संशब्दितं तपः ।\nरजस्तमोघ्नं यत्कर्म तपसस्तत्स्वलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The heat of austerity is knowledge, and in the world austerity is so named; action that destroys rajas and tamas is austerity's own mark."}},{"n":17,"text":"ब्रह्मचर्यमहिंसा च शारीरं तप उच्यते ।\nवाङ्मनोनियमः साम्यं मानसं तप उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Continence and non-violence are called bodily austerity; restraint of speech and mind, and evenness, are called mental austerity."}},{"n":18,"text":"विधिज्ञेभ्यो द्विजातिभ्यो ग्राह्यमन्नं विशिष्यते ।\nआहारनियमेनास्य पाप्मा नश्यति राजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Food taken from twice-born men who know the rules is especially good; by regulated eating one's sin of rajas is destroyed."}},{"n":19,"text":"वैमनस्यं च विषये यान्त्यस्य करणानि च ।\nतस्मात्तन्मात्रमादद्याद्यावदत्र प्रयोजनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His senses lose their taste for objects; so he should take just as much as is needed here."}},{"n":20,"text":"अन्तकाले वयोत्कर्षाच्छनैः कुर्यादनातुरः ।\nएवं युक्तेन मनसा ज्ञानं तदुपपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Near the end, as his age advances, he should proceed slowly, free of distress; so, with a mind joined thus, that knowledge arises."}},{"n":21,"text":"रजसा चाप्ययं देही देहवाञ्शब्दवच्चरेत् ।\nकार्यैरव्याहतमतिर्वैराग्यात्प्रकृतौ स्थितः ।\nआ देहादप्रमादाच्च देहान्ताद्विप्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though embodied, through rajas he moves as if tied to words, his mind unhindered by tasks, established in nature through dispassion; he is freed from the body, careful until the end of the body."}},{"n":22,"text":"हेतुयुक्तः सदोत्सर्गो भूतानां प्रलयस्तथा ।\nपरप्रत्ययसर्गे तु नियतं नातिवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Creation and dissolution of beings are always bound by cause; yet in creation by another's cause, it keeps within the fixed bounds."}},{"n":23,"text":"भवान्तप्रभवप्रज्ञा आसते ये विपर्ययम् ।\nधृत्या देहान्धारयन्तो बुद्धिसंक्षिप्तमानसाः ।\nस्थानेभ्यो ध्वंसमानाश्च सूक्ष्मत्वात्तानुपासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those whose insight into the origin and end of becoming remains inverted, holding their bodies by steadiness, with minds focused by intellect, falling from their places, worship that very subtle thing."}},{"n":24,"text":"यथागमं च तत्सर्वं बुद्ध्या तन्नैव बुध्यते ।\nदेहान्तं कश्चिदन्वास्ते भावितात्मा निराश्रयः ।\nयुक्तो धारणया कश्चित्सत्तां केचिदुपासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the tradition says, all that is not truly grasped by the mind. Some, of trained self and without support, follow it until the body's end; some, joined with concentration, worship existence."}},{"n":25,"text":"अभ्यस्यन्ति परं देवं विद्युत्संशब्दिताक्षरम् ।\nअन्तकाले ह्युपासन्नास्तपसा दग्धकिल्बिषाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They meditate on the supreme god, the imperishable called lightning; near the end, their sins burnt away by austerity,"}},{"n":26,"text":"सर्व एते महात्मानो गच्छन्ति परमां गतिम् ।\nसूक्ष्मं विशेषणं तेषामवेक्षेच्छास्त्रचक्षुषा ॥","meaning":{"en":"all these great souls go to the highest goal. One should look at the fine distinctions among them with the eye of scripture."}},{"n":27,"text":"देहं तु परमं विद्याद्विमुक्तमपरिग्रहम् ।\nअन्तरिक्षादन्यतरं धारणासक्तमानसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know the highest body to be the one released and without possessions, different from space, its mind attached to concentration."}},{"n":28,"text":"मर्त्यलोकाद्विमुच्यन्ते विद्यासंयुक्तमानसाः ।\nब्रह्मभूता विरजसस्ततो यान्ति परां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those whose minds are joined with knowledge are freed from the mortal world; becoming Brahman, free of rajas, they then go to the highest goal."}},{"n":29,"text":"कषायवर्जितं ज्ञानं येषामुत्पद्यतेऽचलम् ।\nते यान्ति परमाँल्लोकान्विशुध्यन्तो यथाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those in whom unshaken knowledge arises, free of impurity, go to the highest worlds, being purified according to their strength."}},{"n":30,"text":"भगवन्तमजं दिव्यं विष्णुमव्यक्तसंज्ञितम् ।\nभावेन यान्ति शुद्धा ये ज्ञानतृप्ता निराशिषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The pure who, with devotion, go to the lord, the unborn, divine Vishnu named the unmanifest, are content with knowledge and without wishes."}},{"n":31,"text":"ज्ञात्वात्मस्थं हरिं चैव निवर्तन्ते न तेऽव्ययाः ।\nप्राप्य तत्परमं स्थानं मोदन्तेऽक्षरमव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having known Hari within the self, those imperishable ones do not return; reaching that supreme place, they rejoice in the imperishable, unchanging one."}},{"n":32,"text":"एतावदेतद्विज्ञानमेतदस्ति च नास्ति च ।\nतृष्णाबद्धं जगत्सर्वं चक्रवत्परिवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"This much is this knowledge: it is, and it is not. The whole world, bound by craving, turns round like a wheel."}},{"n":33,"text":"बिसतन्तुर्यथैवायमन्तःस्थः सर्वतो बिसे ।\nतृष्णातन्तुरनाद्यन्तस्तथा देहगतः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the fibre of a lotus stalk lies within it throughout the stalk, so the thread of craving, without beginning or end, always dwells in the body."}},{"n":34,"text":"सूच्या सूत्रं यथा वस्त्रे संसारयति वायकः ।\nतद्वत्संसारसूत्रं हि तृष्णासूच्या निबध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a weaver draws thread through cloth with a needle, so the thread of rebirth is fastened with the needle of craving."}},{"n":35,"text":"विकारं प्रकृतिं चैव पुरुषं च सनातनम् ।\nयो यथावद्विजानाति स वितृष्णो विमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who truly knows the transformation, nature and the eternal spirit, freed of craving, is liberated."}},{"n":36,"text":"प्रकाशं भगवानेतदृषिर्नारायणोऽमृतम् ।\nभूतानामनुकम्पार्थं जगाद जगतो हितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord, the sage Narayana, spoke this light, this immortal truth, out of compassion for beings, for the good of the world."}}]}]}